1. Singleton Pattern
Purpose: Ensures only one instance of a class exists.


public class Singleton {

private static volatile Singleton instance;
	//Without volatile, JVM may reorder instructions:
	Internally:
		1. Allocate memory
		2. Assign reference
		3. Initialize object
	Due to optimization, step 2 may happen before step 3.
	Another thread may get a partially initialized object.
	volatile prevents this issue.
	

 private Singleton() {}

 
public static Singleton getInstance() {
if (instance == null) { // First Check
synchronized (Singleton.class) {
if (instance == null) { // Second Check

instance = new Singleton();
}
}
}
}

